1
00:04:48,888 --> 00:04:54,888
In Oz, nothing is what it seems.

2
00:09:37,777 --> 00:09:43,777
Oz the Great and Powerful is a fantasy, adventure,
family film directed by Sam Raimi.

3
00:14:26,666 --> 00:14:32,666
Oscar Diggs, a small-time circus illusionist and con-artist, is whisked from Kansas to the Land of Oz where the
inhabitants assume he's the great wizard of prophecy, there to save Oz from the clutches of evil.

4
00:19:15,555 --> 00:19:21,555
Oz, played by James Franco.

5
00:24:04,444 --> 00:24:10,444
Theodora / Wicked Witch of the West, played by Mila Kunis.

6
00:28:53,333 --> 00:28:59,333
Evanora, played by Rachel Weisz.

7
00:33:42,222 --> 00:33:48,222
Annie / Glinda, played by Michelle Williams.

8
00:38:31,111 --> 00:38:37,111
Frank / Finley, played by Zach Braff.

9
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:26,000
Master Tinker, played by Bill Cobbs.

10
00:48:08,888 --> 00:48:14,888
Oz the Great and Powerful is a 2013 American fantasy adventure film directed by Sam Raimi and
written by David Lindsay-Abaire and Mitchell Kapner, from a story by Kapner.

11
00:52:57,777 --> 00:53:03,777
Based on L.

12
00:57:46,666 --> 00:57:52,666
Frank Baum's early 20th century Oz books and set 20 years before the events of the original 1900 novel,
the film is a spiritual prequel to the 1939 Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer film The Wizard of Oz.

13
01:02:35,555 --> 01:02:41,555
Starring James Franco in the title role, Mila Kunis, Rachel Weisz, Michelle Williams, Zach Braff, Bill Cobbs, Joey King, and Tony Cox; the film tells the story of Oscar Diggs, a deceitful  stage
magician who arrives in the Land of Oz and encounters three witches: Theodora, the Good Witch of the North, Evanora, the Wicked Witch of the East, and Glinda, the Good Witch of the South.

14
01:07:24,444 --> 01:07:30,444
Diggs is then enlisted to restore order in Oz while struggling to
resolve conflicts with the witches and himself.

15
01:12:13,333 --> 01:12:19,333
It is Disney's third film adaptation of Baum's works, following Return to Oz
(1985) and the television film The Muppets' Wizard of Oz (2005).

16
01:17:02,222 --> 01:17:08,222
Kapner began developing an origin story for the Wizard of Oz after a
lifelong interest in wanting to create one for the character.

17
01:21:51,111 --> 01:21:57,111
Walt Disney Pictures commissioned the film's production in 2009 with Joe Roth as producer and Grant
Curtis, Joshua Donen, Philip Steuer and Palak Patel serving as executive producers.

18
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
Raimi was hired to direct the following year.

19
01:31:28,888 --> 01:31:34,888
After Robert Downey Jr.

20
01:36:17,777 --> 01:36:23,777
and Johnny Depp declined the title role in January
and February 2011, Franco was cast.

21
01:41:06,666 --> 01:41:12,666
Filming took place from July to December 2011.

22
01:45:55,555 --> 01:46:01,555
Danny Elfman composed the music score for the film.

23
01:50:44,444 --> 01:50:50,444
Oz the Great and Powerful premiered at the El Capitan Theatre in Los Angeles on February 13, 2013, and was released
theatrically in the United States on March 8, 2013, in Disney Digital 3-D, RealD 3D and IMAX 3D formats.

24
01:55:33,333 --> 01:55:39,333
It received mixed reviews from critics and was commercially successful, grossing $493.3 million
worldwide and becoming the highest-grossing Oz-related film until Wicked (2024).

25
02:00:22,222 --> 02:00:28,222
The film won the Phoenix Film Critics Society Award for Best Live Action Family Film and Kunis won the
MTV Movie Award for Best Villain for her performance as the Wicked Witch of the West.

26
02:05:11,111 --> 02:05:17,111
The film explores themes of witch, based on novel or book, magic, circus, hope.
